1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,390
Greek Island Holidays, can I help you?

2
00:00:02,390 --> 00:00:04,476
Yes, I hope so.

3
00:00:04,476 --> 00:00:07,512
I have a friend who's just come back from Corfu

4
00:00:07,512 --> 00:00:10,073
and she's recommended some apartments in Arilas.

5
00:00:10,073 --> 00:00:13,000
She thought they might be on your list.

6
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,782
Arilas, Arilas, let me see.

7
00:00:15,782 --> 00:00:19,120
Can you give me the names?

8
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:21,327
Yes, the first's Rose Garden Apartments.

9
00:00:21,327 --> 00:00:26,110
I'd like to go with another friend in the last week of October.

10
00:00:26,110 --> 00:00:31,560
Well, we've got a lovely studio flat available at that time.

11
00:00:31,560 --> 00:00:36,497
I'm sure you'd enjoy the entertainment programme there too, with Greek dancing in the

12
00:00:36,497 --> 00:00:36,850
restaurant.

13
00:00:36,850 --> 00:00:39,150
And the cost for each of us?

14
00:00:39,150 --> 00:00:41,500
219.

15
00:00:41,500 --> 00:00:43,300
That sounds very reasonable!

16
00:00:43,300 --> 00:00:46,000
I'm just jotting down some notes.

17
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:50,500
Now the second one she mentioned was called Blue Bay.

18
00:00:50,500 --> 00:00:51,619
Blue Bay?

19
00:00:51,619 --> 00:00:58,330
Yes, in fact that's very popular and it has some special features.

20
00:00:58,330 --> 00:00:58,810
Really?

21
00:00:58,810 --> 00:01:03,000
The main attraction is the large swimming pool with salt water.

22
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:05,150
Much healthier, I understand.

23
00:01:05,150 --> 00:01:05,949
That's right.

24
00:01:05,949 --> 00:01:10,341
And it isn't far from the beach, either -only 300 metres,

25
00:01:10,341 --> 00:01:13,935
and only around healf a kilometre to some shops,

26
00:01:13,935 --> 00:01:17,130
so you don't have to be too energetic.

27
00:01:17,130 --> 00:01:19,780
Is it much more expensive than the first one?

28
00:01:19,780 --> 00:01:21,875
Let me just check.

29
00:01:21,875 --> 00:01:28,685
I think at the time you want to go it's around 260 - no

30
00:01:28,685 --> 00:01:30,780
275 to be exact.

31
00:01:30,780 --> 00:01:32,296
Right, I've got that.

32
00:01:32,296 --> 00:01:36,466
Now there are just two more apartments to ask you about.

33
00:01:36,466 --> 00:01:39,120
Um, I can't read my own writing!

34
00:01:39,120 --> 00:01:42,000
Something to do with sun…Sunshine, is it?

35
00:01:42,000 --> 00:01:45,093
I think you meant the Sunshade Apartments.

36
00:01:45,093 --> 00:01:46,860
They're on a mountainside.

37
00:01:46,860 --> 00:01:48,540
Any special features?

38
00:01:48,540 --> 00:01:54,290
Yes, each room has its own sun terrace and there are shared barbecue facilities.

39
00:01:54,290 --> 00:01:55,570
Sounds lovely!

40
00:01:55,570 --> 00:01:57,968
Yes, it is rather well-equipped.

41
00:01:57,968 --> 00:02:02,762
It also provides water sports - it has its own beach.

42
00:02:02,762 --> 00:02:05,160
There are facilities for water-skiing.

43
00:02:05,160 --> 00:02:06,193
Any kite-surfing?

44
00:02:06,193 --> 00:02:08,260
My friend's quite keen.

45
00:02:08,260 --> 00:02:13,148
Not at the hotel but I'm sure you'll find some in Arilas.

46
00:02:13,148 --> 00:02:16,000
There's also satellite TV in the apartments.

47
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:17,550
And how much is that one?

48
00:02:17,550 --> 00:02:21,840
490 with two sharing.

49
00:02:21,840 --> 00:02:24,850
You mean 245 each?

50
00:02:24,850 --> 00:02:25,848
I'm afraid not!

51
00:02:25,848 --> 00:02:30,502
Each person has to pay that amount and there must be at least two

52
00:02:30,502 --> 00:02:31,500
in an apartment.

53
00:02:31,500 --> 00:02:35,095
I don't think that would be within our budget, unfortunately.

54
00:02:35,095 --> 00:02:39,050
And the last one sounds a bit expensive too- the Grand!

55
00:02:39,050 --> 00:02:40,806
Actually it's quite reasonable.

56
00:02:40,806 --> 00:02:45,634
It's an older style house with Greek paintings in every room,

57
00:02:45,634 --> 00:02:47,390
and a balcony outside.

58
00:02:47,390 --> 00:02:48,041
Sounds nice.

59
00:02:48,041 --> 00:02:49,670
What are the views like?

60
00:02:49,670 --> 00:02:54,416
Well, there are forests all round and they hide a supermarket just down the

61
00:02:54,416 --> 00:02:54,755
road,

62
00:02:54,755 --> 00:02:57,807
so that's very useful for all your shopping needs.

63
00:02:57,807 --> 00:03:00,180
There's a disco in the area too.

64
00:03:00,180 --> 00:03:01,230
And the price?

65
00:03:01,230 --> 00:03:03,260
319 at that time,

66
00:03:03,260 --> 00:03:09,350
but if you leave it till November it goes down by 40%.

67
00:03:09,350 --> 00:03:11,180
Too late, I'm afraid.

68
00:03:11,180 --> 00:03:16,090
Well, why don't I send you a brochure with full details, Ms…?

69
00:03:16,090 --> 00:03:16,394
Nash.

70
00:03:16,394 --> 00:03:20,340
But don't worry about that, I'm coming to Upminster soon and I'll call

71
00:03:20,340 --> 00:03:21,251
and get one.

72
00:03:21,251 --> 00:03:23,680
I just wanted to get an idea first.

73
00:03:23,680 --> 00:03:24,078
Well,

74
00:03:24,078 --> 00:03:24,874
that's fine.

75
00:03:24,874 --> 00:03:27,660
We've got plenty here when you come.

76
00:03:27,660 --> 00:03:31,747
If you've got a minute, could I just check a couple of points about

77
00:03:31,747 --> 00:03:32,039
insurance?

78
00:03:32,039 --> 00:03:36,126
I got one policy through the post but I'd like to see if yours

79
00:03:36,126 --> 00:03:36,710
is better.

80
00:03:36,710 --> 00:03:37,113
Fine.

81
00:03:37,113 --> 00:03:39,530
What would you like to know?

82
00:03:39,530 --> 00:03:44,261
Well, the one I've got has benefits and then the maximum amount you can

83
00:03:44,261 --> 00:03:44,598
claim.

84
00:03:44,598 --> 00:03:45,950
Is that like yours?

85
00:03:45,950 --> 00:03:46,377
Yes,

86
00:03:46,377 --> 00:03:48,940
that's how most of them are.

87
00:03:48,940 --> 00:03:51,103
Well, the first thing is cancellation.

88
00:03:51,103 --> 00:03:56,150
If the holiday's cancelled on the policy I've got, you can claim 8,000.

89
00:03:56,150 --> 00:03:59,282
We can improve on that, Ms Nash.

90
00:03:59,282 --> 00:04:03,310
For Greek Island holidays, our maximum is 10,000.

91
00:04:03,310 --> 00:04:08,240
That's good - of course our holiday won't even cost 1,000 together!

92
00:04:08,240 --> 00:04:11,342
It's still sensible to have good cover.

93
00:04:11,342 --> 00:04:15,330
Now, if you go to hospital, we allow 600.

94
00:04:15,330 --> 00:04:16,310
Yes, mine's similar.

95
00:04:16,310 --> 00:04:20,410
And we also allow a relative to your holiday resort.

96
00:04:20,410 --> 00:04:23,880
My policy just says their representative will help you.

97
00:04:23,880 --> 00:04:26,145
You can see there's another difference there.

98
00:04:26,145 --> 00:04:29,380
And what happens if you don't get on the plane?

99
00:04:29,380 --> 00:04:32,530
Nothing, as far as I can see on this form.

100
00:04:32,530 --> 00:04:35,960
Don't you have missed departure?

101
00:04:35,960 --> 00:04:39,110
No, I'll just jot that down.

102
00:04:39,110 --> 00:04:44,117
We pay up to 1,000 for that, depending on the reason.

103
00:04:44,117 --> 00:04:49,125
And we're particularly generous about loss of personal belongings-up to 3,000,

104
00:04:49,125 --> 00:04:52,880
but not more than 500 for a single item.

105
00:04:52,880 --> 00:04:54,910
Then I'd better not take my laptop!

106
00:04:54,910 --> 00:04:57,230
Not unless you insure it separately.

107
00:04:57,230 --> 00:05:00,545
OK-thanks very much for your time-you've really been helpful.

108
00:05:00,545 --> 00:05:02,755
Can I get back to you?

109
00:05:02,755 --> 00:05:03,860
Your name is?

110
00:05:03,860 --> 00:05:05,059
Ben-Ludlow.

111
00:05:05,059 --> 00:05:07,458
That's L-U-D-L-O-W.

112
00:05:07,458 --> 00:05:13,455
I'm the Assistant Manager here.

113
00:05:13,455 --> 00:05:19,451
I'll give you my number.

114
00:05:19,451 --> 00:05:21,850
It's 081260543216.

115
00:05:21,850 --> 00:05:25,654
But didn't I phone 081260567294?

116
00:05:25,654 --> 00:05:30,980
That's what I've got on the paper.

117
00:05:30,980 --> 00:05:32,444
That's the main switchboard.

118
00:05:32,444 --> 00:05:34,640
I've given you my direct line.

119
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:37,220
Right, thank you…
